  11. Patents.

  A "patent contributor" is a party that contributes to a covered work
the claims of a patent owned by that party, which are necessarily
infringed by that party's own action in conveying the work.  A "patent
license" is any agreement or licensor, expressed or implied, to
forbid or permit the use of the patent by others.  A patent contributor
grants to the conveyors and recipients of the covered work a non-exclusive
license, to the extent of the patent's claims, to make, use, sell, offer
for sale, import and export the covered work and its derivatives.

  If you, or a party you associate with, conveys a covered work that
relies on a patent you own or control, and you do not grant to the
recipients a patent license for the claims of that patent, then the
recipients of your conveyance have the right to demand from you a
patent license for that patent.  If you refuse, you must cease
conveying that covered work until the dispute is resolved.

